{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>You</b> — He has mentioned the heavens and the holy ones, which none but the wise understand. Now he returns to mention His might in visible things, namely the sea." "<b>in pride</b> — in its surging." "<b>You still them</b> — You quiet them, like משביח." "<b>You</b> — It is possible that the sense of תשבחם is on account of Israel, the sea." "And the sense of דכאת כחלל רהב — they are Egypt, and the meaning is the men of Rahab."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 89, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:36:28.227096442Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}